        <section id="planning-stage"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>Planning stage</h2>
              <p>The planning stage incorporates two stages - Gathering and analysis; and Design.</p>
<p>See below to learn more about these two stages.</p>

              
              
  <div class="toggle-group">
  
<toggle-section open="false">
    
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Gathering and analysis
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <ol>
<li>Meeting between the client, senior members of the IT team, and business analyst.</li>
<li>The project manager guides discussions to outline the specific needs of the client/end user.</li>
<li>The aim is to produce a software requirement specification (SRS) document which outlines the economic, operational, and technical details.</li>
</ol>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u1_s3_p2_accordion1.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
</toggle-section>
  
<toggle-section open="false">
    
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Design
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <ol>
<li>With reference to the SRS, the project manager and IT team will develop a design document specification (DDS) which outlines roadmaps to project completion, including the programming languages and modules which are required.</li>
<li>This may include the use of flow diagrams or pseudocode to draft out the software architecture.</li>
<li>The DDS is then reviewed by the main stakeholders, and when an approach is decided the details of technical approaches and data flow are outlined.</li>
</ol>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/uc/uc_u1_s3_p2_accordion2.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
</toggle-section>
  
<toggle-section open="false">
    <h3>Importance of the planning stage</h3>
    <p>Planning is the most important and fundamental stage as it requires senior members of the programming team to liaise with the customer to determine feasibility, and outline commercial, technical, and operational aspects of the project.</p>
<p>Once the design stage is completed, this forms the foundation from which the subsequent stages of the SDLC will run, and so must be executed carefully in order to minimize risks and ensure successful project implementation.</p>

</toggle-section>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
